<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>License for Artifacts</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All datasets used in this work are publicly available and free to use on HuggingFace. All <span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLM</span>s are used in accordance with the licenses released by their respective developing organizations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Usage of AI Assistants</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We only use AI Assistants to assist our writing to identify grammar errors, typos and rephrase terms for readability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Computational Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LLaMA-3.1-Instruct (8B, 70B), LLaMA-3.2-Instruct (3B), LLaMA-3.3-Instruct (70B), Mistral Instruct (8x22B), Yi-1.5-Chat (6B, 9B, 34B) and DeepSeek-R1 (Qwen 32B) were all run on eight NVIDIA:RTXA5000 GPUs and were allocated a total of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math> GPU hours to run all experiments. All OpenAI models were run on CPU and were allocated a total of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> hours to run all experiments. Each <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLM</span> decodes with a maximum token generation length of 50, to ensure no extra verbiage is generated. We did not perform a hyperparameter search. All results are obtained from a single run.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For generating the rationales as mentioned in <a href="#S2" title="2 Rationale Generation ‣ Everything is Plausible: Investigating the Impact of LLM Rationales on Human Notions of Plausibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we set temperature to be <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> for GPT-4o. For generating plausibility ratings as discussed in <a href="#S4" title="4 Do Rationales Affect LLMs as well? ‣ Everything is Plausible: Investigating the Impact of LLM Rationales on Human Notions of Plausibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we set temperature to be <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> for OpenAI models and Non-OpenAI models respectively to ensure greedy decoding.</p>
</div>
