<td id="A1.T5.2.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="A1.T5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\textbf{0.0037}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">0.0037</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\textbf{0.0037}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>OLS regression coefficients for the Rationale Length as a feature for ratings given by Humans, OpenAI and Non-OpenAI models. The dependent variable here is the change <math id="A1.T5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> in the plausibility rating after a rationale was presented. Numbers highlighted in <span id="A1.T5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span> represent coefficients that are statistically significant <math id="A1.T5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p&lt;0.05)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p&lt;0.05)</annotation></semantics></math> according to the t-test.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Annotation Process Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used Prolific to collect the human annotations for all three rationale conditions. The annotators for our task were selected on the basis of the following criteria:</p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Must be located in the United States.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Primary language must be English.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Must not have any literacy difficulties.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Must have attained a minimum of an undergraduate level degree.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Must have an approval rate between <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="99-100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">99-100\%</annotation></semantics></math> on Prolific.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a <math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50-50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50-50</annotation></semantics></math> split of male and female<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  Gender as indicated on Prolific.</span></span></span> annotators to minimize the risk of any gender-specific biases creeping in.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The total cost for our entire human annotations for all three rationales came out to be <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\$1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">$</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\$1000</annotation></semantics></math>. We also received an exempt status from the <span id="A1.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">IRB</span> at our institution for this research. We do not collect any personally identifiable information from the annotators.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Prompts used for Rationale Generation and Plausibility Ratings</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We release the prompts used in our work for generating the rationales and prompting the models for plausibility ratings below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="220.47" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 220.47" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,220.47) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 215.15 C 0 218.09 2.38 220.47 5.32 220.47 L 647.83 220.47 C 650.77 220.47 653.15 218.09 653.15 215.15 L 653.15 5.32 C 653.15 2.38 650.77 0 647.83 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 197.1 L 651.77 197.1 L 651.77 5.32 C 651.77 3.15 650 1.38 647.83 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#666666;" fill="#666666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 198.48 L 1.38 215.15 C 1.38 217.32 3.15 219.09 5.32 219.09 L 647.83 219.09 C 650 219.09 651.77 217.32 651.77 215.15 L 651.77 198.48 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.53 205.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.4em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="642.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.4em;">
<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt A.1: PRO Rationale Generation Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.53 5.53)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.4em;--ltx-fo-height:13.54em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="187.42" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 187.42)" width="642.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.4em;">
<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Give your best rationale as to why the given choice is a plausible answer for the question. The rationale should not be more than 2 sentences long and should be concise. Your rationale has to be in favour of the plausibility of the choice, no matter what. Some of these situations may require creativity or thinking outside to box to come up with a rationale that best explains the plausibility of the answer choice. Feel free to be as creative as required.
<br class="ltx_break">Question:<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> <math id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Choice:<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> <math id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Generated Rationale:<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> <span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-bg-color:#800080;">PRO<span id="A1.SS5.p2.pic1.2.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> Rationale</span></span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="220.47" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 220.47" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,220.47) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 215.15 C 0 218.09 2.38 220.47 5.32 220.47 L 647.83 220.47 C 650.77 220.47 653.15 218.09 653.15 215.15 L 653.15 5.32 C 653.15 2.38 650.77 0 647.83 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 197.1 L 651.77 197.1 L 651.77 5.32 C 651.77 3.15 650 1.38 647.83 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#666666;" fill="#666666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 198.48 L 1.38 215.15 C 1.38 217.32 3.15 219.09 5.32 219.09 L 647.83 219.09 C 650 219.09 651.77 217.32 651.77 215.15 L 651.77 198.48 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.53 205.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.4em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="642.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.4em;">
<span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt A.2: CON Rationale Generation Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.53 5.53)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.4em;--ltx-fo-height:13.54em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="187.42" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 187.42)" width="642.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.4em;">
<span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Give your best rationale as to why the given choice is an implausible answer for the question. The rationale should not be more than 2 sentences long and should be concise. Your rationale has to be in favour of the implausibility of the choice, no matter what. Some of these situations may require creativity or thinking outside to box to come up with a rationale that best explains the implausibility of the answer choice. Feel free to be as creative as required.
<br class="ltx_break">Question:<span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> <math id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Choice:<span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> <math id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Generated Rationale:<span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> <span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-bg-color:#ED1C24;">CON<span id="A1.SS5.p3.pic1.2.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> Rationale</span></span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="286.89" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 286.89" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,286.89) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.32 L 0 281.57 C 0 284.51 2.38 286.89 5.32 286.89 L 647.83 286.89 C 650.77 286.89 653.15 284.51 653.15 281.57 L 653.15 5.32 C 653.15 2.38 650.77 0 647.83 0 L 5.32 0 C 2.38 0 0 2.38 0 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 5.32 L 1.38 263.52 L 651.77 263.52 L 651.77 5.32 C 651.77 3.15 650 1.38 647.83 1.38 L 5.32 1.38 C 3.15 1.38 1.38 3.15 1.38 5.32 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#666666;" fill="#666666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.38 264.9 L 1.38 281.57 C 1.38 283.74 3.15 285.5 5.32 285.5 L 647.83 285.5 C 650 285.5 651.77 283.74 651.77 281.57 L 651.77 264.9 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.53 271.74)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.4em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="642.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.4em;">
<span id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt A.3: Plausibility Rating Without Rationales</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 5.53 5.53)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.4em;--ltx-fo-height:18.34em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="253.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 253.84)" width="642.05"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.4em;">
<span id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I will give you a question and an answer choice. Your task is to rate the plausibility of the answer choice on the following Likert scale: 
<br class="ltx_break">Likert Scale:
<br class="ltx_break">1 - Impossible
<br class="ltx_break">2 - Technically Possible
<br class="ltx_break">3 - Plausible
<br class="ltx_break">4 - Likely
<br class="ltx_break">5 - Very Likely
<br class="ltx_break">Your answer should just be a complete option from the Likert scale. Nothing else. No extra words or explanations.
<br class="ltx_break">Question:<span id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> <math id="A1.SS5.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>
