<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Pro Rationale:</span> Dogs are social animals that thrive on interaction</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">and companionship, making lots of attention essential for their</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">emotional well-being and development. By providing</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">attention, owners can strengthen their bond with their dog,</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">enhance socialization skills, and reduce the risk of behavioral</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">issues stemming from loneliness or neglect.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><span id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Con Rationale:</span> While dogs may enjoy attention, it is not a</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">fundamental need comparable to shelter or regular exercise,</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">making "lots of attention" an implausible equivalent to basic</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">survival necessities.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Human Rating <math id="A1.T9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.T9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.4</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">LLM Rating <math id="A1.T9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> (OpenAI): <math id="A1.T9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.16" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T9.2.3.2.1.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">LLM Rating <math id="A1.T9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> (Non-OpenAI): <math id="A1.T9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.33" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.33</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.33</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>(Continued from <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.5 Prompts used for Rationale Generation and Plausibility Ratings ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Everything is Plausible: Investigating the Impact of LLM Rationales on Human Notions of Plausibility" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 8</span></a>)Examples from <span id="A1.T9.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SIQA</span> and <span id="A1.T9.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CQA</span> showing mean plausibility rating changes for different agents when <span id="A1.T9.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PRO Rationales</span> and <span id="A1.T9.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CON Rationales</span> are shown together.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A1.F4.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.F4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:3.0pt;"><img src="2510.08091v1/figures/preference_interface.png" id="A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/181;" width="476" height="181" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span> An example of the interface that annotators used while choosing the best rationale for an answer choice as described in <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1 Model Preference Study ‣ 2 Rationale Generation ‣ Everything is Plausible: Investigating the Impact of LLM Rationales on Human Notions of Plausibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. Example taken from <span id="A1.F4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SIQA</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A1.F5.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.F5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:3.0pt;"><img src="2510.08091v1/figures/siqa_interface.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/193;" width="476" height="193" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span> An example of the interface that annotators used while giving plausibility ratings to answer choices with a <span id="A1.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PRO</span> rationale as described in <a href="#S3" title="3 Human Plausibility Ratings ‣ Everything is Plausible: Investigating the Impact of LLM Rationales on Human Notions of Plausibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Example taken from <span id="A1.F5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SIQA</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A1.F6.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.F6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:3.0pt;"><img src="2510.08091v1/figures/cqa_interface.png" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/167;" width="476" height="167" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span> An example of the interface that annotators used while giving plausibility ratings to answer choices with a <span id="A1.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CON</span> rationale as described in <a href="#S3" title="3 Human Plausibility Ratings ‣ Everything is Plausible: Investigating the Impact of LLM Rationales on Human Notions of Plausibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Example taken from <span id="A1.F6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CQA</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A1.F7.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.F7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:3.0pt;"><img src="2510.08091v1/figures/cqa_pro_con_interface.png" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/198;" width="476" height="198" alt="Refer to caption"></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span> An example of the interface that annotators used while giving plausibility ratings to answer choices with both <span id="A1.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PRO and CON</span> rationales as described in <a href="#S3" title="3 Human Plausibility Ratings ‣ Everything is Plausible: Investigating the Impact of LLM Rationales on Human Notions of Plausibility" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Example taken from <span id="A1.F7.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CQA</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
